const SYL_EITHER = ['Only I follows', 'Only II follows', 'Either I or II follows', 'Neither I nor II follows'];
const ASM = ['Only I is implicit', 'Only II is implicit', 'Both I and II are implicit', 'Neither I nor II is implicit'];

const RC_UPI = 'In the last few years, digital payments have grown rapidly in India. The Unified Payments Interface, or UPI, allows people to send money instantly using a mobile phone. Small shopkeepers, vegetable sellers and auto drivers now accept payments through QR codes. This has reduced the need to carry cash and has made transactions faster. However, experts warn that users must be careful. Fraudsters often send fake links or ask for PINs over the phone. Banks advise customers never to share their UPI PIN with anyone, because the PIN is needed only to send money, not to receive it.';
const RC_STEPWELL = 'For centuries, people in the dry regions of Rajasthan have depended on stepwells, known locally as baoris, to store rainwater. These deep structures have steps leading down to the water, so people could reach it even when the water level fell in summer. The thick stone walls kept the water cool and reduced evaporation. With the arrival of piped water and borewells, many stepwells were neglected and filled with garbage. Recently, some villages and city groups have started cleaning them again. They believe that old methods of saving rainwater can help solve today\'s water shortage.';
const RC_SOFT = 'Many engineering students believe that good marks alone will get them a job. But recruiters in IT companies look for more than technical knowledge. During interviews, they check whether a candidate can explain ideas clearly, work in a team and handle pressure calmly. A student who knows the answer but cannot express it may lose to someone who communicates well. This is why many colleges now run training sessions on communication, group discussions and mock interviews. Students who practise these skills early often feel more confident when the placement season begins.';
const RC_MILLET = 'The United Nations declared 2023 as the International Year of Millets, an idea proposed by India. Millets such as jowar, bajra and ragi were once common in Indian kitchens. They grow well in dry areas, need much less water than rice or wheat and can survive high temperatures. Millets are also rich in fibre, iron and calcium. Over time, people moved towards polished rice and wheat, and millets came to be seen as "poor man\'s food". Today, nutrition experts and farmers are working together to bring these healthy grains back to our plates.';
const RC_MOON = 'In August 2023, India\'s Chandrayaan-3 mission successfully landed near the south pole of the Moon. India became the first country to land in this region. The lander, named Vikram, carried a small rover called Pragyan, which moved on the lunar surface and studied the soil. Scientists were especially interested in the south pole because some craters there are always in shadow and may contain frozen water. The mission cost much less than many space projects of other nations, which showed that ISRO can achieve big goals with careful planning and limited budgets.';
